summary: Test packaged IPA, nothing built
description: |
    No FreeIPA checkout and no build: the channel images are baked with the
    IPA packages of the guest's own Fedora release (FREEIPA_IPA_FROM_DISTRO,
    see tests/freeipa-env/tf-runner.sh), so the compose of the request picks
    the release under test. A request that sets FREEIPA_IPA_FROM_COPR and
    FREEIPA_COPR_REPOS installs them from those COPR repos instead. The
    presets to run come in FREEIPA_JOBS; `freeipa-env queue run QUEUE
    --runner testing-farm [--copr OWNER/PROJECT]` submits this plan from
    this repository.
discover:
    how: fmf
    test: "^/tmt/tests/"
prepare:
    how: install
    package: [podman, python3-pyyaml]
execute:
    how: tmt
environment:
    FREEIPA_IPA_FROM_DISTRO: "1"
